{"name":"Royal Raisin","hex":"#806f72","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"royal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to a monarch or his (or her) family.","Having the air or demeanour of a monarch; illustrious; magnanimous; of more than common size or excellence."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A royal person; a member of a royal family.","A standard size of printing paper, measuring 25 by 20 inches."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/royal"},{"term":"raisin","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dried grape."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Of fruit: to dry out; to become like raisins.","To flavor (an alcoholic beverage) with fruit that has raisined."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/raisin"}],"entries":[{"title":"Raisin","blocks":[{"text":"A raisin is a dried grape. Raisins are produced in many regions of the world and may be eaten raw or used in cooking, baking, and brewing. The word raisin is commonly used for the dried dark-colored seedless grape, while sultana is a golden-colored dried grape, and currant is a dried small Black Corinth seedless grape."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7d/Raisins_01.jpg/330px-Raisins_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Raisin"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Raisins_2.jpg/500px-Raisins_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2b/Raisins_2.jpg/500px-Raisins_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Golden raisins (sultanas)","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARaisins_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/00/Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg/500px-Grape_Rasins_plus_Zante_Currants.jpg?utm_source